WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.629
Good morning, Hank, it's Tuesday. Yeah, I do say Tuesday weird. Deal with it.

00:00:03.629 --> 00:00:07.170
If you didn't know, I'm the other Nerd Factor winner
known as NerdyandQuirky. Hi.

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:09.630
Following the pattern formed by previous
videos, I am NOT John.

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:13.080
I'm about as not John as possible.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.760
What I am is a fifteen-year-old living
in the modern era,

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:19.740
experiencing teenage life and noticing all the unfortunate things my peers and I do.

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.800
So Hank, I'm here like the ghost in a Dickens novel to warn you about the annoying things

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.600
your niece and nephew might do, at least according to [sing song] stereotypes

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:27.920
[sing song] Oprah hands

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.140
Friends and social life will basically become more
important than anything else.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:34.620
I'm not being exclusive to social interactions
that take place in real life, because

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:39.030
[pffh] that would probably involve going
outside and let's be honest.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:40.590
[as mom] Sabrina, it's time for dinner

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:43.330
Sabrina: [hisses] Not now. Alex and I are rewriting the Book of Mormon.

00:00:43.330 --> 00:00:44.059
"Mom": Whaa-

00:00:44.059 --> 00:00:44.739
Sabrina: I'll eat later

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:49.020
Diets will range from eating no food the whole day to eating all the food in the world.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.220
Let me tell you, if I'm
left to my own devices, I will forget to

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:54.870
eat the whole day. Until the sound of my
stomach growling is louder than the

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:57.780
YouTube video I'm watching. And then I'll microwave something, probably a bag of popcorn.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:01.300
Then I'll eat a bag of chips, then some
crackers, probably some cheese.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:04.920
Then, to counteract how salty that was, I'll
probably eat some ice cream or cake.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:07.140
There's a science to it. The science of delicious.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:11.490
Next, they will fangirl. This affects both [*all]
genders. This fangirling may be talking

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:15.240
about people. Said  people may be older
than you. It's kind of weird but don't

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.200
worry too much about it. [ding]

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:21.680
[orchestral background music]

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.820
Also, there will be a stage in life where
meme quoting is done unironically.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:28.600
I'm staring straight into the Sun because
YOLO.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:30.700
Then it's gonna move to its ironic usage.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:34.440
Made bananas in the toaster. YOLO.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.460
Then this usage will continue, until it once again becomes unironic.

00:01:36.469 --> 00:01:40.060
Catching up on current events. YOLO.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:41.469
There will also be slurred speech.

00:01:41.469 --> 00:01:44.079
[slurred] yeah, so I told him to shut up, because communities are really [unintelligible]

00:01:44.079 --> 00:01:46.390
...understand quality humor...face...right?

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:47.390
You're so right!

00:01:47.390 --> 00:01:48.470
Yeah!

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:49.310
Bad vision.

00:01:49.310 --> 00:01:51.880
You are the prettiest thing I've ever seen in ever. No wait,

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:55.120
I changed my mind you are. No wait, changed my mind again.

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:55.959
Trouble breathing.

00:01:55.959 --> 00:01:56.599
"Mom": How was your day?

00:01:56.599 --> 00:01:58.239
Sabrina: [groans]

00:01:58.239 --> 00:02:00.239
Weird, these are starting to sound
like medicine warnings.

00:02:00.239 --> 00:02:06.099
As if the very act of aging is like taking medicine. The experience is making us more mature and

00:02:06.099 --> 00:02:09.219
intelligent with possible negative side
effects.

00:02:09.219 --> 00:02:13.099
[sobbing]

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:15.540
Did I actually just pull a metaphor out
of that?

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:20.880
Yees I did! [high five] [pff] What do you mean it was a stretch? Excuse you, who do you think I am?

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:24.880
John Green? Hank, I'll see you on Friday.

